From b33a35cd59ec1ba48e26ad470370c97e752ff019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:57:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: core: deselect instead of sleep at shutdown (N950
 eMMC/ubiboot)

At shutdown mmc_shutdown() -> _mmc_suspend(MMC_POWEROFF_SHUTDOWN) put the
card into sleep (CMD5) when it cannot do a power-off notification, as the
N950's Hynix eMMC (ext_csd rev >= 3, no MMC_CAP2_POWEROFF_NOTIFY) cannot.
The card keeps that sleep state over the reboot: the board switches off
VEMMC (the card's VCC) but leaves VCCQ on, and ubiboot's old (2.6.32) MMC
driver then does not wake the card and reports no eMMC, so the user has to
reset a second time to boot. Keeping VEMMC on is no fix either (the card
then stays asleep with no power cycle and Leste's own kexec'd kernel does
not find it).

The card is powered off right after, so sleep buys nothing at shutdown.
Deselect it instead (as a card that cannot sleep is), leaving it in a
state both ubiboot and a kexec'd kernel initialise normally. Suspend is
unchanged. The cache is still flushed first, so no data is lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c
index f9f083d18..d32cc3311 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/mmc.c
@@ -2160,7 +2160,15 @@ static int _mmc_suspend(struct mmc_host *host, enum mmc_poweroff_type pm_type)
 	if (mmc_card_can_poweroff_notify(host->card) &&
 	    mmc_host_can_poweroff_notify(host, pm_type))
 		err = mmc_poweroff_notify(host->card, notify_type);
-	else if (mmc_card_can_sleep(host->card))
+	/*
+	 * At shutdown, deselect the card instead of putting it to sleep
+	 * (CMD5). On the Nokia N950 the Hynix eMMC keeps the sleep state over
+	 * the reboot (VEMMC, its VCC, is switched off while VCCQ stays on), and
+	 * ubiboot's old MMC driver then does not wake it and reports no eMMC.
+	 * The card is powered off next anyway, so sleep buys nothing here.
+	 */
+	else if (pm_type != MMC_POWEROFF_SHUTDOWN &&
+		 mmc_card_can_sleep(host->card))
 		err = mmc_sleep(host);
 	else if (!mmc_host_is_spi(host))
 		err = mmc_deselect_cards(host);
